VISIT CONTEXT

Case ID: HMO-008
Reason for Visit: Acute, heavy vaginal haemorrhage and severe deep pelvic pain requiring urgent assessment for haemodynamic stability and haemostasis.
Location: Private residence
Present at Visit: Patient only
Urgency Justification: Telephone triage reported sudden, unremitting, heavy vaginal bleeding passing large clots, accompanied by new-onset severe pelvic and right flank pain. Urgent in-person evaluation was necessary to evaluate for catastrophic haemorrhage and obstructive uropathy, which posed an immediate life-threatening risk if left unassessed until the next in-hours period.

SUBJECTIVE

Chief Complaint: "I started pouring blood an hour ago with huge clots, and my lower stomach and right back are in absolute agony."
History of Present Illness: The patient reports an insidious 4-month history of persistent, foul-smelling heavy vaginal discharge and intermittent postcoital spotting, which was not investigated. One hour ago, they experienced an abrupt onset of heavy vaginal haemorrhage, soaking a maternity pad every 20 minutes. This is accompanied by severe, deeply localized lower pelvic pain and sharp right-sided flank pain radiating to the groin. The patient also notes significant unintentional weight loss over the past 6 months.
Functional Status: Currently bedbound due to severe pain and fear of exacerbating the bleeding upon standing.
Social/Safety Concerns: Living alone; high risk of syncope from hypovolemia.

OBJECTIVE

